MacaulayPosets -- a package for working with Macaulay posets and Macaulay rings
*******************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package contains a few methods for working with posets, rings, and the
Macaulay property.

Two boolean methods for ranked posets are implemented.

  * *note isAdditive: isAdditive,
  * *note isMacaulay: isMacaulay,, also applicable to rings

Four poset operations and two ring operations are implemented.

  * *note posetWedgeProduct: posetWedgeProduct,, analogous to *note
    ringFiberProduct: ringFiberProduct,
  * *note posetClosedProduct: posetClosedProduct,, analogous to *note
    ringConnectedSum: ringConnectedSum,
  * *note posetFiberProduct: posetFiberProduct,
  * *note posetConnectedSum: posetConnectedSum,

To define the latter two poset operations, a new data type *note PosetMap:
PosetMap, was created.

To obtain the monomial poset of a ring, one can use *note getPoset: getPoset,,
a generalization of *note standardMonomialPoset: (Posets)standardMonomialPoset,
from the *note Posets package: (Posets)Top, to ideals which are not necessarily
monomial.

This package was used in some of the work leading to the paper
https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.15166, where many of these operations and properties
are discussed.

