AllOrders -- whether to return all orders instead of at most one order
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        macaulayOrders(P, AllOrders=>Boolean)

Description
===========

With AllOrders=>false, the list returned by the method will have at most one
element.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = booleanLattice 3                      |
|                                               |
|o1 = B                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : Poset                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : #(macaulayOrders B)                       |
|                                               |
|o2 = 12                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : macaulayOrders(B, AllOrders=>false)       |
|                                               |
|o3 = {{000, 001, 010, 100, 011, 101, 110, 111}}|
|                                               |
|o3 : List                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------+

