isAdditive -- whether a poset is additive
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        isAdditive P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

See section 3.2 of https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.15166 for a definition of
additivity.

Boolean lattices are additive. Therefore, the *note wedge product:
posetWedgeProduct, of a Boolean lattice with itself is Macaulay.

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = booleanLattice 3              |
|                                       |
|o1 = B                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : Poset                             |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : isAdditive B                      |
|                                       |
|o2 = true                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : isMacaulay posetWedgeProduct(B, B)|
|                                       |
|o3 = true                              |
+---------------------------------------+

Here is a non-additive poset.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isAdditive poset({1,2,3,4,5,6}, {{1,2},{1,3},{2,4},{3,4},{3,5},{3,6}})|
|                                                                           |
|o4 = false                                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

