isRankPreserving -- whether a poset map is rank-preserving
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isRankPreserving f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of posets: PosetMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

A *note poset map: PosetMap, $f: P\rightarrow Q$ between *note ranked:
(Posets)isRanked, posets is rank-preserving if and only if, for each $p \in P$,
the rank of $p$ is equal to the rank of $f(p)$, assuming both $P$ and $Q$ have
a rank $0$ element.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : isRankPreserving map(chain 2, chain 1, {1})|
|                                                |
|o1 = true                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isRankPreserving map(chain 2, chain 1, {2})|
|                                                |
|o2 = false                                      |
+------------------------------------------------+

