macaulayOrders -- finds all orders with respect to which the poset is Macaulay
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        macaulayOrders P
        macaulayOrders S
        macaulayOrders I
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, 
      * S, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, a homogeneous
        level linearly independent quotient of a polynomial ring over a field
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal of a
        polynomial ring such that the quotient is level linearly independent
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note TikZ: TikZ, => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to print TikZ code
      * *note Visual: Visual, => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value false, whether to visualize the Macaulay orders
      * *note AllOrders: AllOrders, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, whether to return all
        orders instead of at most one order
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, whose elements are lists
        representing orders with respect to which the poset is Macaulay

Description
===========

Given a poset with rank function $r$, this method returns all Macaulay orders
$<$ on the poset such that $r(p) < r(q)$ implies $p < q$.

Given a quotient $S$ of a polynomial ring, this method returns Macaulay orders
on the monomial poset of $S$.

A total order $<$ on a poset $P$ is represented by a *note list:
(Macaulay2Doc)list,. It is the permutation of the of the ground set of $P$ that
is increasing with respect to $<$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : macaulayOrders(product(chain 3, chain 3))                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {{{1, 1}, {1, 2}, {2, 1}, {1, 3}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}, {2, 3}, {3, 2}, {3,   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     3}}, {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {1, 2}, {3, 1}, {2, 2}, {1, 3}, {3, 2}, {2, 3},   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {3, 3}}}                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The option *note TikZ: TikZ, can print a Hasse diagram of the poset for each
order $<$ such that the vertices in each level are ordered left to right
according to $<$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = (ZZ/2)[x,y]                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal(x^4, x^3-y^3, y^4)                                            |
|                                                                             |
|             4   3    3   4                                                  |
|o3 = ideal (x , x  + y , y )                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : macaulayOrders(R/I, TikZ=>true)                                         |
|                                                                             |
|        \draw (0) -- (1);                                                    |
|        \draw (0) -- (2);                                                    |
|        \draw (1) -- (4);                                                    |
|        \draw (1) -- (3);                                                    |
|        \draw (3) -- (8);                                                    |
|        \draw (3) -- (6);                                                    |
|        \draw (6) -- (9);                                                    |
|        \draw (4) -- (7);                                                    |
|        \draw (4) -- (6);                                                    |
|        \draw (7) -- (9);                                                    |
|        \draw (2) -- (5);                                                    |
|        \draw (2) -- (4);                                                    |
|        \draw (5) -- (8);                                                    |
|        \draw (5) -- (7);                                                    |
|\end{tikzpicture}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|        \draw (0) -- (2);                                                    |
|        \draw (0) -- (1);                                                    |
|        \draw (2) -- (4);                                                    |
|        \draw (2) -- (5);                                                    |
|        \draw (5) -- (8);                                                    |
|        \draw (5) -- (7);                                                    |
|        \draw (7) -- (9);                                                    |
|        \draw (4) -- (6);                                                    |
|        \draw (4) -- (7);                                                    |
|        \draw (6) -- (9);                                                    |
|        \draw (1) -- (3);                                                    |
|        \draw (1) -- (4);                                                    |
|        \draw (3) -- (8);                                                    |
|        \draw (3) -- (6);                                                    |
|\end{tikzpicture}                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|                 2        2   2      2   3   2 2              2        2     |
|o4 = {{1, x, y, x , x*y, y , x y, x*y , y , x y }, {1, y, x, y , x*y, x ,    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2   2    3   2 2                                                     |
|     x*y , x y, y , x y }}                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
