map(Poset,Poset,List) -- make a poset map
*****************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        map(Q, P, L)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, the source
        poset
      * Q, an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, the target
        poset
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of length #(vertices P) and whose
        $i$th entry specifies the image of the $i$th element of P, or a *note
        List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of *note Option: (Macaulay2Doc)Option,s whose
        keys are vertices P and whose values are in vertices Q, or a *note
        HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, whose keys are vertices P and whose
        values are in vertices Q
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of posets: PosetMap,, the poset map from P to Q specified
        by L.

Description
===========

A poset map is a monotone function $f: P\rightarrow Q$ from a poset $P$ to a
poset $Q$, so $f(p)\leq f(q)$ whenever $p\leq q$.

Let $P = [2]$ and $Q = [3] \times [3]$. Here are the three ways to obtain the
map $\phi: P \rightarrow Q$ given by $\phi(1) = (1,1)$ and $\phi(2) = (1,2)$.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = chain 2                                  |
|                                                  |
|o1 = P                                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 : Poset                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q = product(chain 3, chain 3)                |
|                                                  |
|o2 = Q                                            |
|                                                  |
|o2 : Poset                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Q, P, {{1,1}, {1,2}})                |
|                                                  |
|o3 = PosetMap{1 => {1, 1}}                        |
|              2 => {1, 2}                         |
|              source => P                         |
|              target => Q                         |
|                                                  |
|o3 : PosetMap                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = map(Q, P, {1=>{1,1}, 2=>{1,2}})          |
|                                                  |
|o4 = PosetMap{1 => {1, 1}}                        |
|              2 => {1, 2}                         |
|              source => P                         |
|              target => Q                         |
|                                                  |
|o4 : PosetMap                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : h = map(Q, P, hashTable {1=>{1,1}, 2=>{1,2}})|
|                                                  |
|o5 = PosetMap{1 => {1, 1}}                        |
|              2 => {1, 2}                         |
|              source => P                         |
|              target => Q                         |
|                                                  |
|o5 : PosetMap                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f == g                                       |
|                                                  |
|o6 = true                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g == h                                       |
|                                                  |
|o7 = true                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Potentially, some of the vertices of the target may be *note options:
(Macaulay2Doc)Option,. When there is ambiguity, the list elements will be taken
as vertices of the target as in the first of the three ways above.

+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : P = poset({1}, {})               |
|                                      |
|o8 = P                                |
|                                      |
|o8 : Poset                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i9 : Q = poset({1, 1=>1}, {{1, 1=>1}})|
|                                      |
|o9 = Q                                |
|                                      |
|o9 : Poset                            |
+--------------------------------------+
|i10 : f = map(Q, P, {1=>1})           |
|                                      |
|o10 = PosetMap{1 => 1 => 1}           |
|               source => P            |
|               target => Q            |
|                                      |
|o10 : PosetMap                        |
+--------------------------------------+
|i11 : f 1                             |
|                                      |
|o11 = 1 => 1                          |
|                                      |
|o11 : Option                          |
+--------------------------------------+

