posetFiberProduct -- constructs the fiber product of several posets
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        posetFiberProduct L
        posetFiberProduct(f, g)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of rank-preserving
        injective *note PosetMap: PosetMap,s.
      * f, a *note map of posets: PosetMap,, 
      * g, a *note map of posets: PosetMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note Poset: (Posets)Poset,, 

Description
===========

In this construction, several posets are glued together along a common
subposet. Suppose $(A, \leq_A), (B, \leq_B), (C, \leq_C)$ are posets and
$\iota_A: C \rightarrow A$ and $\iota_B: C \rightarrow B$ are rank-preserving,
injective, and monotone. Then, we have a fiber product \[A \times_C B = (A
\setminus \iota_A(C)) \sqcup (B \setminus \iota_B(C)) \sqcup C\] with $a \geq
c$ iff $a \geq_A \iota_A(c)$ for $a \in A$ and $c \in C$, and $b \geq c$ iff $b
\geq_B \iota_A(c)$ for $b \in A$ and $c \in C$.

This is a generalization of *note posetWedgeProduct: posetWedgeProduct,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = product(chain 2, chain 2)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = P                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Poset                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q = product(chain 2, chain 3)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Q                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Poset                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Q, P, {{1,1}, {1,2}, {2,1}, {2,2}})                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = PosetMap{{1, 1} => {1, 1}}                                              |
|              {1, 2} => {1, 2}                                               |
|              {2, 1} => {2, 1}                                               |
|              {2, 2} => {2, 2}                                               |
|              source => P                                                    |
|              target => Q                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : PosetMap                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = map(Q, P, {{1,1}, {2,1}, {1,2}, {2,2}})                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = PosetMap{{1, 1} => {1, 1}}                                              |
|              {1, 2} => {2, 1}                                               |
|              {2, 1} => {1, 2}                                               |
|              {2, 2} => {2, 2}                                               |
|              source => P                                                    |
|              target => Q                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : PosetMap                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = (ZZ/2)[x,y]                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
